# Which thismoon mods Claude Code runs on this machine. Applied by
# sync-mods.sh on every `ralph up`.
#
# One mod per line: <name> <state>. Names are the entries in thismoon's
# .claude-plugin/marketplace.json; a # starts a comment. A line sync-mods.sh
# can't use (a missing or extra word, an unknown state, an on or off mod the
# marketplace doesn't list) is an error, and `ralph doctor` reports it.
#
#   on        install and enable it. The sources cache pull brings its
#             changes, since Claude Code runs it from its folder there.
#             While the install record's version differs from the
#             folder's, `claude plugin update` brings the record in step
#   off       disable it but keep it installed, with its data
#   retired   uninstall it: drops the install record, the enabledPlugins
#             entry and the mod's data folder
#
# A mod that isn't listed here is left alone, so deleting a line changes
# nothing. Mark the mod retired, run `ralph up` on every machine, then delete
# the line.
session-band    on
humanizer-gate  on
panel-policy    off
# loom-pane     retired
